30,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The late-turn pool is dangerously thin, but we do have some capacity in the lift and escalator maintenance contract.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Interestingly, a late-evening pilot worked well years ago, but some previous lane-priority projects were just rolled back.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Working in old stations is a gamble right now due to unrecorded voids. However, roadway consents are much easier to handle.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"We have a ring-fenced construction balance we could use, but our operating subsidy is being cut.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"The mid-city runs are slower, but the crowds aren't the main issue. Most delays happen while waiting for connections.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Daisuke, if the operating subsidy is low, we can't afford a plan that requires massive new staffing.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Sakura, if the delays are in the connections, maybe the mid-city corridor isn't the answer.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, if we avoid the pre-war shells, we avoid the biggest cost risks.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, that makes sense. Using the construction balance for something predictable would be safer.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Takumi, that's true. We should look for something that improves the flow without just adding more buses.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, does the roadway ease mean a bus corridor is more viable than station work?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Takumi,,Only if it doesn't end up like the previous lane-priority failures.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"It depends on the specific route, but the administrative path is definitely clearer.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm worried about the ticketing fees; they are eating into our paving budget.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"If the ticketing system is a mess, maybe that's why connections feel so slow?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
