55,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"Looking at the candidates, the Night Service Extension is impossible with our current roster depletion.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Takumi,,The Crosstown Bus Corridor risks repeating the lane-priority failures I found in the records.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Station Access Upgrades are too risky because of the voids in the pre-war shells.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The Integrated Fare Platform could reduce those contractor fees I saw, but is it ""construction""?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"The Fare Platform doesn't fix the connection wait times, but it simplifies the journey.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"Wait, the Station Access Upgrades align with the maintenance capacity I found for lifts and escalators.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Takumi,,But @Toshio said the shells are a nightmare. That's a huge risk.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Toshio,,Exactly. The Integrated Fare Platform has the fewest physical and administrative hurdles.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"If we can use the ring-fenced construction balance for the Fare Platform's infrastructure, it's the safest bet.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Sakura,,It's better than a bus corridor that might just get removed in five years.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. The Fare Platform doesn't put more pressure on the exhausted late-turn crews.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Takumi,,It's a fresh start that doesn't repeat the specific mistakes of the old bus pilots.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Toshio,,It avoids the pre-war shells and the joint operator disputes over roadway consents.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,It's the most fiscally responsible choice given the subsidy cuts.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Sakura,,Let's go with the Integrated Fare Platform.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
